  "nl_text": "The rschema_0112 database is used to manage the operations of a company, encompassing various aspects of its business, including employee information, product details, customer data, sales performance, and financial transactions. The Employee table stores information about each employee, including their base salary, commission rate, email, employee ID, employee number, hire date, name, office phone, position, and supervisor ID, which references the Employee ID of their supervisor. The Product table contains details about each product, such as its brand, cost price, description, inventory quantity, model, name, product ID, specification, suggested retail price, and supplier. The Order table tracks all orders, including the actual shipping date, notes, order ID, order date, order status, required delivery date, and special instructions. The Office_location table stores information about each office location, including the city, contact phone, country, fax, manager employee ID, which references the Employee ID of the manager, and office location ID. The Customer table contains customer information, including their city, contact person name, contact person phone, contact person position, country, credit limit, customer ID, customer company name, dedicated sales representative employee ID, which references the Employee ID of the sales representative, postal code, state or province, and street address. The Sales_performance_record table tracks the sales performance of each employee, including the record ID, sales person ID, total sales, and year. The Order_detail table links orders to the products they contain, with each entry including the line number, order ID, product ID, quantity, and unit price. The Payment_record table stores payment information, including the check clearing date, check number, customer accounts receivable, invoice amount, paying customer ID, which references the Customer ID of the customer making the payment, payment date, and record ID.",
  "gold_question": "This is a Sales Management System for managing company sales, orders, customers, employees, and products. For office location management, the system manages company office locations including city, street address, postal code, country, records office contact numbers and fax numbers, and assigns dedicated managers for each location. For employee management, the system records employee basic information including name, position, hire date, employee number, maintains employee office phone and email contacts, sets up direct supervisors to establish clear reporting relationships, records employee base salary and commission rates, and tracks sales performance and revenue for each fiscal year. For customer management, the system records customer company names, customer IDs, maintains detailed contact person information including name, position, phone, records detailed addresses including street, city, state/province, postal code, country, assigns dedicated sales representatives for each customer, sets and manages customer credit limits, and records payment details including check numbers, payment dates, and amounts. For product management, the system records product names, models, specifications, descriptions, sets product cost prices and suggested retail prices, tracks inventory quantities, and records product suppliers and brands. For order management, the system records order dates, requested delivery dates, actual shipping dates and ordering customers, tracks order status (such as pending, shipped, completed), records special instructions and notes, and details product quantities, unit prices, and line numbers in each order. For sales performance management, the system records each salesperson's total sales by fiscal year, analyzes sales trends and performance changes, evaluates sales strategy effectiveness, and provides data support for setting sales targets. For payment management, the system records check numbers, payment dates, invoice amounts and paying customers for each payment, registers check clearing dates, and tracks customer accounts receivable.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0112.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0112\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `office_phone` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `base_salary` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `commission_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `hire_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `supervisor_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`supervisor_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `brand` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `model` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `specification` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `cost_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `suggested_retail_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `inventory_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supplier` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `required_delivery_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `actual_shipping_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `special_instructions` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `office_location` (\n  `office_location_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `state_or_province` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `street_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_phone` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `fax` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `manager_employee_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`office_location_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `office_location_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`manager_employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_company_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_person_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_person_phone` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_person_position` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `state_or_province` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `street_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `credit_limit` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `dedicated_sales_representative_employee_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `customer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`dedicated_sales_representative_employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_performance_record` (\n  `record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_person_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_sales` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_performance_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sales_person_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_detail` (\n  `line_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`line_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_detail_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_detail_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `payment_record` (\n  `record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `check_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `check_clearing_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `invoice_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_accounts_receivable` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `paying_customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `payment_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`paying_customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
